}



the const keyword specifies that a variable's value is constant.
tells the compiler to prevent any accidental changes to that variable's value.
(read-only variable)

if someone tries to change the value of pi, the compiler will generate an error, preventing any unintended modifications to the constant variable.
for example,

	double pi = 3.14159;
	pi = 720.99;
	double radius = 10;
	double circumference = 2 * pi * radius;


this will result in different output.

to prevent this, we declare pi as a constant variable using the const keyword as a prefix.

"const double pi = 3.14159;"
